[cot:thought] The issue is case sensitivity or character matching. The CSS `uppercase`
[cot:thought] class makes the visible text all caps, but Playwright's `getByText` uses `innerText`, which returns the uppercase string. This causes the case-sensitive substring search to fail.
[cot:thought] Other posts use similar
[cot:thought] uppercase markers successfully. The mismatch likely stems from CSS rendering differences rather than a universal bug.
[cot:thought] Playwright docs indicate
[cot:thought] getByText is case-insensitive by default, so the failure is unexpected. The middle dot character may be the actual cause.
[cot:thought] The middle dot character
[cot:thought] is identical across visible text, so it is not the cause. Playwright's `getByText` may be reading the original `textContent` instead of the uppercase `innerText`, which would explain why the case-sensitive search fails despite the visual text being all caps.
[cot:thought] The smoke and QA markers
[cot:thought] will be updated to use the headline phrase "0.97 permits per net household". This avoids the uppercase CSS transform and resolves the case-sensitive search failure.
